commit 465f5ec3ffcb33adcb364a227cf3d34b2a68911c
Author: Tony Walteur <tony.walteur@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Jul 11 08:13:15 2026 -0400

    Scope renderer local-readiness gates to the modes each site fires

    Audit round 4 found local-only setups either bounced to Settings on
    local-capable paths or nudged into requests local refuses. Per-site
    audit: the summarize quick action fires summary mode in every non-
    vision branch, so it now accepts localSummaryReady; explain, fact-
    check, what-next, submit and assist keep the bare provider gate
    because each has a direct answer-mode branch that only cloud serves.
    The No-Decision Honk gate returns to providerReady-only — it fires an
    answer-mode request by design, which Métis Local never serves. A new
    source-contract test pins every requireProvider call site's argument
    and the honk gate so future drift fails the suite.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

